@startuml Seat Analyzer - Approaches Comparison
!theme aws-orange

title Seat Vacancy Analyzer - Three Approaches Comparison

skinparam backgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

package "🥉 Approach 1: Enhanced Simulation" as Approach1 {
  rectangle "**QUICK MVP**" as MVP1 #lightgreen {
    + Enhanced seat patterns
    + Realistic simulation
    + Crowd-based occupancy
    + Time-aware logic
    + Route-specific behavior
    + Demo-ready in 1-2 weeks
    
    - No real hardware
    - Limited accuracy
    - No reservations
    - Simulated data only
  }
  
  rectangle "Implementation Effort" as Effort1 #lightblue {
    **Timeline:** 1-2 weeks
    **Cost:** $0 (software only)
    **Complexity:** Low
    **Hardware:** None required
    **Team Size:** 1-2 developers
  }
}

package "🥈 Approach 2: IoT Integration" as Approach2 {
  rectangle "**BALANCED SOLUTION**" as MVP2 #lightyellow {
    + Real sensor data
    + IoT-powered accuracy
    + Real-time seat status
    + Crowd validation
    + Analytics dashboard
    + Production-ready foundation
    
    + Some hardware costs
    + Moderate complexity
    + Sensor maintenance
    + Network dependency
  }
  
  rectangle "Implementation Effort" as Effort2 #lightblue {
    **Timeline:** 4-6 weeks
    **Cost:** $50-100 per bus (sensors)
    **Complexity:** Medium
    **Hardware:** Pressure/weight sensors
    **Team Size:** 2-3 developers + 1 hardware
  }
}

package "🥇 Approach 3: Advanced AI System" as Approach3 {
  rectangle "**COMPLETE SOLUTION**" as MVP3 #lightcoral {
    + AI-powered predictions
    + Seat reservations & payments
    + Personalized recommendations
    + Multi-modal integration
    + Advanced analytics
    + Full ecosystem
    
    + High complexity
    + Significant investment
    + Long development time
    + Multiple integrations
  }
  
  rectangle "Implementation Effort" as Effort3 #lightblue {
    **Timeline:** 3-6 months
    **Cost:** $10,000+ (full system)
    **Complexity:** High
    **Hardware:** IoT + Cloud + ML
    **Team Size:** 5-8 developers + ML engineer
  }
}

rectangle "Feature Comparison Matrix" as Matrix #lightyellow {
  |= Feature |= Approach 1 |= Approach 2 |= Approach 3 |
  | Real-time Updates | ✅ Simulated | ✅ Real IoT | ✅ Real + AI |
  | Seat Reservations | ❌ No | ⚠️ Basic | ✅ Advanced |
  | Payment Integration | ❌ No | ❌ No | ✅ Full |
  | ML Predictions | ⚠️ Basic | ✅ Good | ✅ Advanced |
  | Hardware Required | ❌ None | ✅ Sensors | ✅ Full IoT |
  | Development Time | ✅ 1-2 weeks | ⚠️ 4-6 weeks | ❌ 3-6 months |
  | Cost | ✅ $0 | ⚠️ $2K-5K | ❌ $10K+ |
  | Demo Readiness | ✅ Immediate | ⚠️ Medium | ❌ Long-term |
  | Scalability | ⚠️ Limited | ✅ Good | ✅ Excellent |
  | User Experience | ⚠️ Basic | ✅ Good | ✅ Premium |
}

rectangle "Recommended Evolution Path" as Evolution #lightgreen {
  **Phase 1 (Week 1-2):** Start with Approach 1
  • Build enhanced simulation
  • Create seat map visualization
  • Implement basic analytics
  • Get stakeholder buy-in
  
  **Phase 2 (Month 2-3):** Upgrade to Approach 2
  • Add IoT sensor integration
  • Implement real-time data processing
  • Build production-ready APIs
  • Deploy on pilot routes
  
  **Phase 3 (Month 4-6):** Evolve to Approach 3
  • Add AI/ML capabilities
  • Implement seat reservations
  • Add payment integration
  • Scale to full city network
}

note bottom of Evolution
  **Smart Strategy:** 
  Start simple, prove value, then scale up!
  Each phase builds on the previous one.
end note

@enduml
